      17. In the 6 months prior to enrollment, patients had been arteriovenous thrombosis (AVT), such as cerebrovascular accident (including temporary ischemic attack, cerebral hemorrhage, cerebral infarction), deep vein thrombosis (DVT) and pulmonary embolism;
